 Rolled back checkout-api in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Post-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate the root cause in v2.3.1 before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 18650, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Q3Q5WfMVguJAvCtx6ctxaK", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18650, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q3Q5WfMVguJAvCtx6ctxaK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 22409, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened a SEV2 incident describing what I did.\n\n- **The problem:** v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with 18% of requests returning errors. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging before it went out.\n- **The rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **The incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) covers the failure, the rollback and the current healthy state. It asks for the root cause in v2.3.1 to be found before it's redeployed. The on-call engineer has been paged. There were no existing incidents, so this isn't a duplicate.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01B4MHKU3ZLmH4hTQAng5qho", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.9