thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened a SEV2 incident describing what I did.\n\n- **The problem:** v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with 18% of requests returning errors. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging before it went out.\n- **The rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **The incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) covers the failure, the rollback and the current healthy state. It asks for the root cause in v2.3.1 to be found before it's redeployed. The on-call engineer has been paged. There were no existing incidents, so this isn't a duplicate.", "type": "text"}]}]}